Please rephrase and refined below: 

As per section 23 of the Sales Tax Act, 1990, a registered person making a taxable supply shall issue a serially numbered tax invoice at the time of supply of goods containing particulars: 

a)	name, address and registration number of the supplier; 
b)	name, address and registration number of the recipient and in case of supplies by manufacturer or importer to unregistered distributor, the NIC or NTN of such unregistered distributors, as the case may.
c)	date of issue of invoice;
d)	description including count, denier and construction in case of textile yarn and fabric, and quantity of goods; 
e)	value exclusive of tax; 
f)	amount of sales tax; and 
g)	value inclusive of tax:

In this respect, it is requested to immediately involved your IT team to make necessary changes in the current invoicing system to ensure the aforesaid mention particulars of sales tax invoices. As indicate above, if the proposed amendment is approved then OUP SMC is required invoice sales tax invoices from July 1, 2024. 

Please note that no person other than a registered person shall issue an invoice. Therefore, OUP SMC is first need to obtain registration then you will be able to raise sales tax invoice.
